Question: Confucius synthesized the great achievements of all the sages and edited and transmitted the Six Classics; among his great deeds and achievements, none surpassed the Spring and Autumn Annals (Chunqiu). In what is recorded in the Spring and Autumn Annals, the conduct of rulers and ministers, both admirable and evil, is fully revealed. Master Zhu [Zhu Xi] synthesized the great achievements of the various Confucian scholars and put the multitude of books into proper order; in his method of instructing people, nothing took precedence over the Elementary Learning (Xiaoxue). In what is recorded in the Elementary Learning, fine words and good deeds provide both encouragement and admonition in full measure. Coming down to our Dynasty…

